Dear Ms. Stanhope,<br />
<br />
This firm represents Torvane Industrial Group, Inc. The attached letter pre=
sents Torvane's claim against Prescott Vane LLP arising from the firm's rep=
resentation of the company in connection with the Kelling Station Unit 2 ex=
pansion project under your Matter 2011-0284.<br />
<br />
In brief: by engagement letter dated April 4, 2011, Prescott Vane undertook=
 to represent Torvane "in connection with claims arising out of the Kelling=
 Station Unit 2 expansion project." Among those claims was a substantial wa=
rranty claim against Brandt Thermal Systems, Inc., supplier of the Unit 2 r=
egenerative thermal oxidizer, whose chronic underperformance is documented =
in the company's own August 2013 engineering study, attached in relevant pa=
rt. Prescott Vane never advised the company of the limitations period appli=
cable to that claim, never acted to preserve it, and allowed it to expire n=
o later than 2015. The company discovered the loss in 2024, in the course o=
f a post-acquisition review of legacy claims.<br />
<br />
Torvane's damages are $3,675,000, comprising $2,140,000 in excess natural-g=
as consumption through fiscal 2013, $890,000 in premature ceramic media rep=
lacement, and $645,000 in unplanned downtime - the value of the claim your =
firm was engaged to protect and did not.<br />
<br />
We ask that you place your professional liability carrier on notice and res=
pond within forty-five days.<br />
<br />
Alan Garvey<br />
Garvey Strom LLP
